---
description: Guidelines for using Nuxt UI MCP tools to get up-to-date component documentation and examples
globs: **/*.vue
alwaysApply: true
---

- **Using Nuxt UI MCP Information:**
  - When working with Nuxt UI components, use MCP tools to get up-to-date documentation
  - Always check MCP documentation before implementing or modifying Nuxt UI components
  - Reference: [design-rules.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/design-rules.mdc) for design system guidelines

- **Available MCP Tools for Nuxt UI:**
  - `mcp_nuxt-ui_list_components` - List all available Nuxt UI components
  - `mcp_nuxt-ui_get_component` - Get detailed component documentation
  - `mcp_nuxt-ui_get_component_metadata` - Get component props, slots, and events
  - `mcp_nuxt-ui_list_composables` - List available composables
  - `mcp_nuxt-ui_get_documentation_page` - Get documentation by URL path
  - `mcp_nuxt-ui_list_examples` - Browse component examples
  - `mcp_nuxt-ui_get_example` - Get specific example implementation code
  - `mcp_nuxt-ui_search_components_by_category` - Search components by category or text

- **When to Use MCP Tools:**
  - **Before implementing a new component** - Check available props, slots, and events
  - **When unsure about component API** - Get exact prop names, types, and default values
  - **To find examples** - See how components are used in practice
  - **To verify component capabilities** - Check what features and variants are available
  - **When debugging component issues** - Verify correct prop usage and available options
  - **To discover alternative components** - Find components that might better fit the use case

- **Recommended Workflow:**
  ```vue
  <!-- 1. List components to find what's available -->
  <!-- Use: mcp_nuxt-ui_list_components -->
  
  <!-- 2. Get specific component details -->
  <!-- Use: mcp_nuxt-ui_get_component with componentName: "UButton" -->
  
  <!-- 3. Get component metadata for props/slots -->
  <!-- Use: mcp_nuxt-ui_get_component_metadata with componentName: "UCard" -->
  
  <!-- 4. Check examples for implementation patterns -->
  <!-- Use: mcp_nuxt-ui_get_example with exampleName -->
  
  <!-- 5. Implement component following MCP documentation -->
  <UButton 
    color="primary" 
    variant="solid"
    size="md"
  >
    Action
  </UButton>
  ```

- **Component Implementation Best Practices:**
  - Always verify prop names match MCP documentation exactly
  - Check available variants and colors before using custom styling
  - Use component slots as documented in MCP metadata
  - Follow examples from MCP when implementing complex component patterns
  - Reference MCP documentation in code comments when using non-standard props

- **Common Use Cases:**
  - **Buttons:** Check available colors, variants, sizes, and icon support
  - **Cards:** Verify header/footer slots and styling options
  - **Forms:** Check form field components, validation props, and input types
  - **Navigation:** Discover breadcrumb, menu, and navigation components
  - **Layout:** Find container, grid, and layout components
  - **Feedback:** Check alert, notification, and modal components
